"program_narrative": "Program ERRPROC is a batch-callable common subroutine that records an error reported by a calling program. It receives an error request (program ID, category, error code, severity, text and details) through its LINKAGE SECTION, takes the current timestamp, and appends one record to the sequential ERROR-LOG file (opened in EXTEND mode). It then prints the same error as a formatted block of DISPLAY lines and returns the caller's severity as the return code. There is no loop; the program runs once per call. Error conditions handled: a non-'00' file status after opening or writing the log is displayed, but processing continues and the program still returns normally. Note: the timestamp source (ACCEPT ... FROM TIME STAMP) is non-standard and the 26-character value is truncated into an 18-byte field.",
